```ts
import {
  canonicalizeClass,
  canonicalizeClasses,
  canonicalizeFile,
  canonicalizeProject,
  canonicalizeSource,
  findCanonicalEquivalent,
  defineConfig,
  createDefaultTheme,
  loadProjectTheme,
  createTailwindCompileEqual,
  watchProject,
} from "tailwind-canonicalize";
```

## findCanonicalEquivalent

```ts
const match = findCanonicalEquivalent("w-[40px]");
// { canonical: "w-10", reason: "theme-exact", ... } | null
```

## canonicalizeClass / canonicalizeClasses

```ts
canonicalizeClass("w-[40px]"); // "w-10"
canonicalizeClasses(["w-[40px]", "flex"]); // ["w-10", "flex"]
```

## canonicalizeSource

```ts
const result = canonicalizeSource(source, {
  filePath: "Card.tsx",
  migrations: true,
});
// { code, changed, transformations, diagnostics }
```

## canonicalizeProject

```ts
const summary = await canonicalizeProject({
  paths: ["src"],
  write: true,
  mode: "safe",
  incremental: true,
  workers: "auto",
});
```

## Theme loading

```ts
const { theme, source } = await loadProjectTheme(process.cwd());
// source: "css" | "v3-config" | "default"
```

## defineConfig

```ts
import { defineConfig } from "tailwind-canonicalize";

export default defineConfig({
  tailwind: { version: 4 },
  canonicalize: { arbitraryValues: true },
});
```

## Transformation records

Every rewrite includes:

```ts
{
  category: "canonical-class" | "tailwind-migration" | "semantic-color-token" | ...,
  original: string,
  replacement: string,
  confidence: "exact" | "high" | "medium" | "low",
  safety: "safe" | "review" | "aggressive",
  token?: string,
  file?: string,
  line?: number,
}
```

Biome formats and lints. Canonicalize rewrites Tailwind semantics. Run both.

```json
{
  "scripts": {
    "fix": "tailwind-canonicalize . --write --safe && biome check --write .",
    "check": "tailwind-canonicalize . --check && biome ci ."
  }
}
```

With Ultracite:

```json
{
  "scripts": {
    "fix": "tailwind-canonicalize . --write --safe && ultracite fix",
    "check": "tailwind-canonicalize . --check && ultracite check"
  }
}
```

Recommended order: **canonicalize first**, then Biome, so format runs on canonical classes.

```json
{
  "scripts": {
    "fix": "tailwind-canonicalize . --write --safe && eslint . --fix",
    "check": "tailwind-canonicalize . --check && eslint ."
  }
}
```

Use `eslint-plugin-tailwindcss` for **class order / invalid names** if you want — not for arbitrary→scale rewrites. That is this tool’s job.

lint-staged:

```json
{
  "*.{js,jsx,ts,tsx}": [
    "tailwind-canonicalize --write",
    "eslint --fix --max-warnings=0"
  ]
}
```

```json
{
  "scripts": {
    "check": "tailwind-canonicalize . --check && oxlint ."
  }
}
```

Oxlint is a reporter; keep rewrites on the canonicalize CLI. Jobs can run in parallel in CI.
